# Source of truth for the light_dbr17_all umbrella CI lock
# (classic DBR 17.3–18 LTS, full feature set, protobuf-5).
# No dedicated CI job — lock exists for users who install geobrix[light_dbr17_all] or
# geobrix[light_dbr18_all] on classic DBR 17.3 / 18 LTS.
#
# Regenerate (from python/geobrix/):
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#       --output-file requirements-light-dbr17-all-ci.txt requirements-light-dbr17-all-ci.in
#
# This .in uses a local-package-with-extra reference so uv expands [light_dbr17_all]
# directly from pyproject.toml. The [light_dbr17_all] extra pulls [light_dbr17]+[stac]+[vizx]+[overture].
# [light_dbr17] caps mapbox-vector-tile<2.2 (protobuf-5; classic DBR 17.3–18).
# [light_all] (env v6 / Serverless) twin: see requirements-light-all-ci.in.
# [light_dbr19_all] (protobuf-6 / classic DBR 19) twin: see requirements-light-dbr19-all-ci.in.
#
# Note: CI resolves without Serverless grpcio-status constraints; the protobuf version
# in this lock (5.x) reflects the [light_dbr17] cap on mapbox-vector-tile, NOT a CI grpcio
# constraint. The real runtime protobuf is set at cluster install time.

# Local package — expands geobrix[light_dbr17_all] from pyproject.toml
.[light_dbr17_all]
